import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner hp = new Scanner(System.in);

        int n = hp.nextInt();
        int m = hp.nextInt();

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int sum = 0;

            for (int j = 0; j < m; j++) {
                int fuel = hp.nextInt();
                sum = sum + fuel;
            }

            System.out.println(sum);
        }

        hp.close();
    }
}


Problem 1 of 2: Car Fuel Efficiency Calculator
Given C cars and M modes, each car has a fuel consumption value for every mode. Calculate and output the total fuel consumed by each car across all modes.
Input Format
The first line contains two integers C (number of cars) and M (number of modes).
The next C lines contain M integers, representing the fuel consumed by each car in different modes.
Output Format
Output the total fuel consumed for each car.
Constraints
1 ≤ C ≤ 50
1 ≤ M ≤ 5
1 ≤ fuel ≤ 100
Example 1
Input
3 3
12 15 18
10 20 25
8 16 24
Output
45
55
48
